{
    "_comment": [
        "QuickSite language list — INSTALL-WIDE.",
        "",
        "This is the shipped list. To change it on this installation, copy it to",
        "languages.json beside this file and edit the copy: the copy is gitignored and,",
        "when it exists, it is the list the engine reads. Never edit this .example.",
        "",
        "One entry per language, \"code\": \"name\". The code is the language's ISO 639 code",
        "as the web writes it: its two-letter ISO 639-1 code, or its three-letter ISO",
        "639-2 / 639-3 code when it has no two-letter one — 2 or 3 lowercase letters.",
        "The name is the language's own name for itself, shown wherever QuickSite shows",
        "the language: letters with their accents and vowel signs, spaces, hyphens,",
        "apostrophes, dots, parentheses and the Tibetan syllable mark, at most 100 bytes.",
        "An entry that breaks either rule is ignored; a copy that is not a JSON object",
        "is ignored whole, and this shipped list is used. Keys starting with _ are comments.",
        "",
        "A language can be added to a project only when its code is in this list.",
        "Removing an entry stops offering it; a project that already has it keeps it.",
        "",
        "Most names come from the Unicode CLDR, version 45 — see languages.NOTICE.txt."
    ],
